## How do I know if my vehicle qualifies for a California lemon law claim?

Vehicles sold with manufacturer or dealership warranties may be eligible for California lemon law claims - assuming the warranty was in effect when the state’s qualifications were met. Warranty terms vary by brand. Most provide 3-year/36,000-mile warranties with new vehicles. Be sure to check your warranty terms.

As long as the defect in question was first reported to the manufacturer while the warranty was in effect, your claim may be valid.

