## Is it possible to pursue an El Cajon lemon law claim without an attorney?

Yes. You always have the option to manage your own California lemon law claim.

However, your odds of receiving fair compensation without an experienced California lemon law attorney go drastically down. Auto brands have many tricks and tactics to avoid legal responsibility for selling lemon vehicles.

An El Cajon lemon law lawyer knows these tactics - and will make sure you don’t fall victim to them during negotiations.

Hiring a California lemon law attorney means you have a professional on your side fighting for every last dollar - and making sure the manufacturer doesn’t delay the process.

## What is the time limit to file a CA lemon law claim?

California lemon law has a four-year statute of limitations for consumers to file a claim with the manufacturer. You are wise to file the claim as soon as possible - as the longer you wait, the more difficult your case will be.

Moreover, it’s extremely dangerous to drive a defective vehicle around.

## What if I want a vehicle replacement over a lemon law buyback?

Some consumers are loyal to their auto brand - and understand that mistakes happen. If you are one of these people, you may request a replacement of the same vehicle or one of equal value. However, the manufacturer is not legally required to provide a replacement (unlike a buyback) and must agree to these terms.

## What if I bought my car in a private sale?

Unfortunately, most private car sales have no protection under California lemon law. These transactions are typically carried out under an “as is” agreement. However, if the vehicle’s warranty is still in effect, the seller may transfer the warranty to your name - and you may be eligible for benefits.

## How long do CA lemon law claims take to resolve?

Every lemon law case is slightly different - and timelines can vary based on many factors. If you hire a skilled California lemon law attorney, they will do everything in their power to resolve the claim as quickly as possible. Generally, most lemon law claims can be resolved in a few weeks to a few months.
